  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests pass now: 2 of 2.\n\nThe bug was in `src/vat.js`. `withVat` used `Math.floor(pence * 1.2)`, which truncates instead of rounding. For 999 pence, 999 × 1.2 = 1198.8, so the function returned 1198 when the comment and the test both expect 1199. I changed it to `Math.round`. The existing 1000 → 1200 and 250 → 300 assertions still hold.\n\nI didn't commit the change; it's a one-line edit in the working tree.",
